invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: the group loop XORs its four blocks last to first. In place each
  16 bytes are still read before they are written, so the output stays
  right there; with the output 5 bytes below the input, as rec_open
  decrypts over its header, the fourth block's first write lands on the
  last 5 input bytes of the third before they are read. chacha20.h allows
  that shape, and bin/chacha20_equiv_test runs it at every length.

--- old
    for (size_t b = 0; b < 4; b++) {
        for (size_t g = 0; g < 4; g++) {
            size_t offset = CHACHA20_BLOCK * b + 16 * g;
--- new
    for (size_t b = 4; b-- > 0;) {
        for (size_t g = 0; g < 4; g++) {
            size_t offset = CHACHA20_BLOCK * b + 16 * g;
